[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2912285765","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106863#issuecomment-2912285765","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106863","id":2912285765,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6tlfRF","user":{"login":"lawnjelly","id":21999379,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxOTk5Mzc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21999379?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly","html_url":"https://github.com/lawnjelly","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-27T12:14:04Z","updated_at":"2025-05-27T12:28:43Z","body":"Just to check, as I haven't looked through thoroughly, but are you handling the case where physics interpolation is off?\r\nWe aim to make behaviour the same as before when physics interpolation is off.\r\n\r\nIs a good start though. :+1: \r\n\r\nIt would also be good to get some input from @godotengine/rendering whether they are happy with this being done CPU side or whether they prefer in a shader (particularly for large soft bodies).\r\n\r\nGranted the soft body itself is being calculated CPU side already, so that's probably the lions share of the bottlenecks. I personally think it would be fine CPU side especially to get started, as it's far less invasive.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2912285765/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2912551698","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106863#issuecomment-2912551698","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106863","id":2912551698,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6tmgMS","user":{"login":"beicause","id":75941842,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc1OTQxODQy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/75941842?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause","html_url":"https://github.com/beicause","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-27T13:37:43Z","updated_at":"2025-05-27T13:37:43Z","body":">Just to check, as I haven't looked through thoroughly, but are you handling the case where physics interpolation is off?\r\nWe aim to make behaviour the same as before when physics interpolation is off.\r\n\r\nIt is handled in:\r\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/7f1387674f3b52619f89284ca824f98ba4482bd9/scene/3d/physics/soft_body_3d.cpp#L322\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/7f1387674f3b52619f89284ca824f98ba4482bd9/scene/3d/physics/soft_body_3d.cpp#L94","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2912551698/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2915337775","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106863#issuecomment-2915337775","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106863","id":2915337775,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6txIYv","user":{"login":"lawnjelly","id":21999379,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxOTk5Mzc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21999379?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly","html_url":"https://github.com/lawnjelly","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-28T07:54:02Z","updated_at":"2025-05-28T07:54:02Z","body":"Sorry BTW if it sounds like there are a lot of changes, you are doing great here. :+1: ","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2915337775/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2924055977","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106863#issuecomment-2924055977","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106863","id":2924055977,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6uSY2p","user":{"login":"beicause","id":75941842,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc1OTQxODQy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/75941842?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause","html_url":"https://github.com/beicause","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-31T02:41:44Z","updated_at":"2025-06-01T15:56:47Z","body":">During the first tick, all SoftBodies are positioned at the global world origin. They move to the correct position on the second physics tick. Is there a way we could avoid this?\r\n\r\nFixed.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2924055977/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2933579128","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106863#issuecomment-2933579128","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106863","id":2933579128,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6u2t14","user":{"login":"lawnjelly","id":21999379,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxOTk5Mzc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21999379?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly","html_url":"https://github.com/lawnjelly","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-03T05:52:08Z","updated_at":"2025-06-03T06:21:58Z","body":"Afaik This still will cause performance regression when physics interpolation off as I said above.\r\n\r\n1) With fti off, it is done per tick whereas most should be done per frame, I.e. it is updating needlessly now. This should be fixed imo, it should be obvious how to fix but if not I have some changes to show how to fix when I get home.\r\n\r\nThe pivots can be updated per tick, but the rendering server should not be, this will be particularly expensive.\r\n\r\n2) There may be a regression with moving objects on the frame and a delay introduced (need to check).\r\n\r\nTLDR - the physics interpolation is now working great, but i'm concerned we've borked it for users who are not using physics interpolation :grin:","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2933579128/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2934695804","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106863#issuecomment-2934695804","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106863","id":2934695804,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6u6-d8","user":{"login":"beicause","id":75941842,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc1OTQxODQy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/75941842?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause","html_url":"https://github.com/beicause","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-03T11:00:37Z","updated_at":"2025-06-03T11:00:37Z","body":">With fti off, it is done per tick whereas most should be done per frame, I.e. it is updating needlessly now\r\n\r\nIsn't frame rate always higher than physical tick rate? Updating per tick is correct in my opinion.\r\n\r\n>The pivots can be updated per tick, but the rendering server should not be, this will be particularly expensive.\r\n\r\nAssuming you are referring to soft_body_update_rendering_server(), it actually doesn't update rendering server, only updates the handler (i.e., the buffers in memory).\r\n\r\n>There may be a regression with moving objects on the frame and a delay introduced (need to check).\r\n\r\nMoving is done in TRANSFORM_CHANGED, and this PR doesn't affect it.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2934695804/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2934790908","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106863#issuecomment-2934790908","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106863","id":2934790908,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6u7Vr8","user":{"login":"lawnjelly","id":21999379,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxOTk5Mzc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21999379?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly","html_url":"https://github.com/lawnjelly","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-03T11:27:57Z","updated_at":"2025-06-03T11:58:07Z","body":"> Isn't frame rate always higher than physical tick rate?\r\n\r\nNo, we can't make that assumption.\r\n\r\nEven with default 60 TPS, frame rate may be slower on slow rendering especially on low power PCs / mobile.\r\nWith e.g. racing games, TPS is often set higher than refresh rate.\r\n\r\nConversely there is also the situation where refresh rate is higher than tick rate, e.g. high refresh rate monitors with good GPU.\r\n\r\nIdeally we would update render server before each frame only, but ignore the update if there had been no physics ticks since the previous frame.\r\n\r\nAs an aside, I noticed that the attachments prior to this PR were previously _not_ updated on the physics tick (on the frame) and that is likely a mistake / bug, so these probably should be done on the tick (as you are doing here).\r\n\r\nI'll try and have a look at this properly when I get home (hopefully this evening). I do realize we are under time pressure a little with feature freeze for 4.5, so if necessary we can merge as is and fix the updating as a follow up. Usually we try and prevent merging with known regressions (or worse putting out builds as such) as it can affect user expectations.\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2934790908/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2940521746","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106863#issuecomment-2940521746","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106863","id":2940521746,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6vRM0S","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-04T15:42:25Z","updated_at":"2025-06-04T15:42:25Z","body":"Thanks!","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2940521746/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":1,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]